      "text": "To determine the value of \\( a - b \\) for the line \\( y = ax + b \\) that passes through the points \\( (4, 5) \\) and \\( (8, 17) \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute the points into the equation \\( y = ax + b \\):**\n\n   For the point \\( (4, 5) \\):\n   \\[\n   5 = a \\cdot 4 + b\n   \\]\n   This gives us the first equation:\n   \\[\n   4a + b = 5 \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\n   \\]\n\n   For the point \\( (8, 17) \\):\n   \\[\n   17 = a \\cdot 8 + b\n   \\]\n   This gives us the second equation:\n   \\[\n   8a + b = 17 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Solve the system of linear equations:**\n\n   We have:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{cases}\n   4a + b = 5 \\\\\n   8a + b = 17\n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n\n   Subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2 to eliminate \\( b \\):\n   \\[\n   (8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   8a + b - 4a - b = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4a = 12\n   \\]\n   Solve for \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Substitute \\( a = 3 \\) back into Equation 1 to solve for \\( b \\):**\n\n   \\[\n   4(3) + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   12 + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = 5 - 12 = -7\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate \\( a - b \\):**\n\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( a - b \\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
