      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the equation \\(y = ax + b\\) given the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), we start by substituting these points into the line equation.\n\nFirst, substitute the point \\((4,5)\\) into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\):\n\\[ 5 = 4a + b \\]\nThis gives us the first equation:\n\\[ 5 = 4a + b \\]\n\nNext, substitute the point \\((8,17)\\) into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\):\n\\[ 17 = 8a + b \\]\nThis gives us the second equation:\n\\[ 17 = 8a + b \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n\\[ 5 = 4a + b \\]\n\\[ 17 = 8a + b \\]\n\nTo eliminate \\(b\\), subtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[ 17 - 5 = 8a + b - (4a + b) \\]\n\\[ 12 = 4a \\]\n\\[ a = \\frac{12}{4} \\]\n\\[ a = 3 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 3\\), substitute it back into the first equation to solve for \\(b\\):\n\\[ 5 = 4(3) + b \\]\n\\[ 5 = 12 + b \\]\n\\[ b = 5 - 12 \\]\n\\[ b = -7 \\]\n\nWe previously found \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\). Now, we need to find \\(a - b\\):\n\\[ a - b = 3 - (-7) \\]\n\\[ a - b = 3 + 7 \\]\n\\[ a - b = 10 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\\boxed{10}\\]",
